          "sid": "modals-t1-s01",
          "c": "我想去香港。",
          "j": "ngo5 soeng2 heoi3 hoeng1 gong2.",
          "e": "I want to go to Hong Kong.",
          "note": "想 (soeng2) + a verb is \"want to / would like to\" — 想去 (soeng2 heoi3) \"want to go\". It's the gentle, polite \"want\"; 要 (jiu3) is the firmer \"need to / must\".",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "我想",
              "j": "ngo5 soeng2",
              "e": "I want to"
            },
            {
              "c": "去",
              "j": "heoi3",
              "e": "go"
            },
            {
              "c": "香港",
              "j": "hoeng1 gong2",
              "e": "Hong Kong"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sid": "modals-t1-s02",
          "c": "你可以幫我嗎？",
          "j": "nei5 ho2 ji5 bong1 ngo5 maa3?",
          "e": "Can you help me?",
          "note": "可以 (ho2 ji5) is \"can / may\" in the sense of being allowed or possible — 你可以幫我嗎？(nei5 ho2 ji5 bong1 ngo5 maa3?) \"can you help me?\". Different from 識 (sik1) \"know how to\" and 會 (wui5) \"will\".",
