    "2": {
      "note": "Tier-2 modals shift from single-verb frames to how modals combine and how permission, willingness, and polite requests work in real situations. Key contrasts: 俾 (bei2) vs 准 (zeon2) for allowing/permitting; 唔肯 (m4 hang2) vs 唔想 (m4 soeng2) for refusal; 好似 (hou2 ci5) for hedging; 實 (sat6) for emphasis. Use 可唔可以 (ho2 m4 ho2 ji5) and 唔該 (m4 goi1) together for polite requests.",
      "words": [
        {
          "id": "modals-014",
          "c": "俾",
          "j": "bei2",
          "e": "To give / to let / to allow"
        },
        {
          "id": "modals-015",
          "c": "唔俾",
          "j": "m4 bei2",
          "e": "To not allow / won't let"
        },
        {
          "id": "modals-016",
          "c": "准",
          "j": "zeon2",
          "e": "To permit / to allow (formal)"
        },
        {
          "id": "modals-017",
          "c": "唔准",
          "j": "m4 zeon2",
          "e": "Not permitted / not allowed"
