        {
          "sid": "modals-t2-s05",
          "c": "如果你唔識，應該問吓，唔使扮識。",
          "j": "jyu4 gwo2 nei5 m4 sik1, jing1 goi1 man6 haa5, m4 sai2 ban6 sik1.",
          "e": "If you don't know how, you should just ask — no need to pretend you do.",
          "note": "扮識 (ban6 sik1) is a natural collocation — 扮 (ban6) means pretend or act as, so 扮識 (ban6 sik1) is pretend to know how. The sentence stacks two tier-1 modals: 應該 (jing1 goi1) should + 唔使 (m4 sai2) no need to.",
          "bd": [
            {
              "c": "如果",
              "j": "jyu4 gwo2",
              "e": "if"
            },
            {
              "c": "你唔識",
